    "long_instructions": "## Analyze Patterns\r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Look through the `animals` array.\r\n2. Count how many animals of each `species` appear.\r\n3. Look at the `gender` field across the dataset.\r\n4. Compare the `bio` field across animals.\r\n\r\n### **Reflect:**\r\n- Which type of animal appears most often?\r\n- Which type appears least?\r\n- What patterns do you notice in the gender of the animals?\r\n- Which animals have more detailed bios? Which have less?",
    "project_template_level_name": "template_building-data-driven-systems-lesson5-level1_choicea_2026",
    "start_sources": {
      "folders": {
      },
      "files": {
      },
      "openFiles": [

      ]
    },
    "teacher_markdown": "### **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n**Students may focus on individual animals instead of looking for patterns**\r\n\r\nSome students will read each animal profile one at a time without stepping back to compare the data across the dataset. Encourage them to summarize their observations by asking: **\"What do you notice when you compare multiple animals of the same species?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant properties:\r\n```javascript\r\nspecies\r\ngender\r\nbio\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students move from reading records to identifying trends.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may confuse observations with conclusions**\r\n\r\nStudents may jump to conclusions without checking the entire dataset. Encourage them to support their answers with evidence by asking: **\"How many animals of each species did you count?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant property:\r\n```javascript\r\nspecies\r\n```\r\n\r\nRemind students that data analysis starts with observations before making claims.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may overlook differences in bio length and detail**\r\n\r\nSome students will focus on species and gender but ignore the descriptive text. Encourage them to compare the bios by asking: **\"Which bios provide the most information about the animal's personality or needs?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant property:\r\n```javascript\r\nbio\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students recognize that not all data fields contain the same amount of information.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may assume the dataset is perfectly balanced**\r\n\r\nStudents may expect equal numbers of species or genders and overlook imbalances. Ask: **\"Are some categories represented more often than others?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant properties:\r\n```javascript\r\nspecies\r\ngender\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis can lead to useful discussions about how datasets are collected and whether they fully represent a population."
  },
